course: dictionary
lesson: 13417
title: Hinny: a horse-donkey cross and a word of love
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. Look at the clues around it to see which meaning fits. «The hinny stood in the field next to the donkey, looking like a small mule.» The clues are donkey and mule, so a hinny is a cross between a horse and a donkey.
explain: «"Alright, hinny?" said the lady in the shop, smiling at Mia.» No animal is nearby. The clues are the smile and the friendly greeting, so hinny here is a loving word, like honey or pet.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning. Here, «hinny» in the shop means a friendly name for Mia, not a young animal.
fact: A hinny is the young of a male horse and a female donkey.
fact: A hinny looks a bit like a mule, which is also a cross between a horse and a donkey.
fact: A mule has a donkey dad and a horse mum; a hinny has a horse dad and a donkey mum.
fact: Hinnies are rarer than mules and usually cannot have babies.
fact: In northern England and Scotland, especially the North East, «hinny» is a loving word for someone, like «honey» or «pet».
exercise: «The hinny stood in the field next to the donkey.» What is a hinny? | A small brown bird | A kind of wooden fence | A very fast kind of car | *A cross between a horse and a donkey
exercise: «"Thanks, hinny, that was kind," said Grandma.» What does hinny mean here? | A young horse | A field full of hay | *A loving word, like honey or pet | A donkey with a bad temper
exercise: Ella says a hinny is just a mule. What is the difference? | A hinny has a donkey dad and a horse mum | A hinny is always bigger than a horse | There is no difference at all | *A hinny has a horse dad and a donkey mum
test: «The hinny was too tired to carry the bags up the hill.» What kind of animal is a hinny? | A cow and a sheep mixed | A bird that cannot fly | A type of goat | *A cross between a horse and a donkey
test: Which statement about hinnies is true? | *They usually cannot have babies | They are more common than mules | They live only in the sea | They have a donkey dad and a horse mum
exam: «"Nearly there, hinny," said Dad as Sam climbed the hill.» What does hinny mean here? | A donkey | A type of cake | *A loving word, like honey or pet | A young horse
